      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "Jesus explained that ordinary water only satisfies thirst for a little while — you'll always need more. But the water he gives works differently: once someone receives it, they are satisfied for good. He also told her that God isn't looking for people who follow the right rituals in the right building; he's looking for people who worship him honestly, from the heart.",
          "ko": "예수님은 보통 물은 잠깐만 갈증을 해결해줄 뿐, 계속 다시 마셔야 한다고 설명하셨습니다. 하지만 그분이 주시는 물은 다릅니다 — 한 번 받으면 다시는 목마르지 않습니다. 그분은 또한 하나님이 정해진 장소와 절차를 따르는 사람을 찾으시는 게 아니라, 진심으로 정직하게 예배하는 사람을 찾으신다고 말씀하셨습니다."
        },
        {
          "text": "God is searching for exactly that kind of worshiper. Later, when his followers urged him to eat something, Jesus pointed out toward the countryside and told them not to wait around — the harvest was ready right now, so there was no reason to delay the work.",
          "ko": "하나님은 바로 그런 예배자를 찾고 계십니다. 나중에 제자들이 뭔가 좀 드시라고 권하자, 예수님은 들판 쪽을 가리키며 더 이상 기다릴 필요 없다고, 추수할 때가 바로 지금이니 일을 미룰 이유가 없다고 말씀하셨습니다."
        },
        {
          "text": "Because of what the woman told them, a lot of people from that town came out to meet Jesus themselves — and once they heard him speak, even more of them put their trust in him.",
